>> title: Carnitas, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: pork, mexican, tacos, braise, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: carnitas
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: taco de carnitas, carnitas taco, roast pork, instant pot carnitas, pressure cooker carnitas
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, salsa-roja, refried-beans
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the ten minutes under the broiler go from crisp edges to dry shreds inside a minute, and the fat is back in the pot
>> step.2: toss with the salt and spice
>> step.3: brown 12 min, in three batches
>> step.4: 45 min high pressure, natural release 15 min
>> step.5: shred, crisp under the broiler 10 min

The pot does the tender and the broiler does the crust. The cup of water is a minimum: below it the pot never seals.

Toss @pork shoulder{4%lb}(1.8 kg; cut in 2-in chunks), @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp} and leave the surface dry.

Brown @&(~1)seasoned pork{} in @lard{2%Tbs} on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~brown{12%min}, in three batches — the pot's element is small and narrow, and four pounds crowded in at once steams instead.

Pressure cook @&(~1)browned pork{} with @orange{1}(halved, squeezed in and dropped in), @white onion{1}(quartered), @garlic{6%cloves}, @bay leaves{2}, @water{1%cup}(240 mL), lid on and valve sealed: ~come to pressure{12%min}, then ~pressure cook{45%min} on high and ~natural release{15%min}.

Shred @&(~1)braised pork{} coarsely, spread it on a sheet with a few spoonfuls of the fat from the top of the pot, and crisp it under the #broiler{} for ~broil{10%min}, watching it — this leg is unchanged from the plain way and it is where carnitas becomes carnitas.
